index 0000000..2161bee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy with Kamal
+
+The included `config/deploy.yml` runs Fizzy on **one Linux server**. The web app,
+Solid Queue workers (including recurring tasks), SQLite databases, and uploaded
+files share one application container. Kamal runs a separate proxy container to
+provide automatic HTTPS certificates from Let's Encrypt. No MySQL, Redis, S3,
+or separate job server is required.
+
+## Before you start
+
+- Fork and clone the repo. On your development machine, install the Ruby version
+  in `.ruby-version`, run `bundle install`, and have Docker running with Buildx
+  available. Kamal builds the repo's production `Dockerfile` locally.
+- Have a Linux server with Docker installed and SSH access. Kamal uses `root` by
+  default. To use another user, add `ssh: { user: deploy }` to `config/deploy.yml`
+  and ensure that user can run Docker without sudo.
+- Point your hostname's DNS A record (and AAAA record, if present) at that server.
+  Ports **80 and 443** must be reachable from the internet for HTTPS certificate
+  issuance and traffic; SSH must be reachable from your development machine.
+  Nothing else should be listening on ports 80 and 443.
+- Create a Docker Hub repository and an access token with push/pull permissions.
+  Both your development machine and the server must be able to reach the registry.
+- Have an SMTP server and an authorized sender address. Fizzy uses emailed codes
+  to sign in, so working outbound mail is required.
+
+## Configure your fork
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml`:
+
+1. Replace `fizzy.example.com` under `servers.web` with your hostname, without
+   `https://` or a path. The YAML alias reuses it for the proxy and `APP_FQDN`, so
+   generated links use that same hostname over HTTPS.
+2. Set `image` to your Docker Hub image (for example, `yourname/fizzy`) and
+   `registry.username` to your Docker Hub username. For another registry, also
+   set `registry.server` and use the appropriate image name and credentials.
+3. Set `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, and `SMTP_DOMAIN` to
+   your provider's values. The example uses authenticated SMTP on port 587 with
+   STARTTLS. `SMTP_DOMAIN` is the domain used in the SMTP HELO/EHLO greeting.
+4. Change `builder.arch` to `arm64` if your server is ARM-based. The default is
+   `amd64`. Web and job concurrency start at one each to suit a small server;
+   increase them if your server has capacity.
+
+Create your local secrets file:
+
+```sh
+cp .kamal/secrets.example .kamal/secrets
+chmod 600 .kamal/secrets
+bin/rails secret
+```
+
+Fill in `.kamal/secrets` with:
+
+- `KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD`: your registry access token, not your account password.
+- `SECRET_KEY_BASE`: the output of `bin/rails secret`. Generate it **once** and
+  retain it across deploys so signed cookies and links remain valid. This fork
+  does not need a `RAILS_MASTER_KEY` unless you add encrypted Rails credentials.
+- `SMTP_USERNAME` and `SMTP_PASSWORD`: your SMTP credentials.
+
+Use single quotes around secret values containing special characters. The local
+secrets file is ignored by Git and excluded from Docker builds. You can also
+reference environment variables in it, e.g. `SMTP_PASSWORD=$SMTP_PASSWORD`.
+Keep a secure backup of your secrets; do not commit them.
+
+### Other mail setups
+
+For implicit TLS (usually port 465), set `SMTP_PORT: 465`, `SMTP_TLS: "true"`, and
+`SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO: "false"` under `env.clear`. TLS and STARTTLS must not
+both be enabled.
+
+For an SMTP relay that does not require authentication, remove `SMTP_USERNAME`
+and `SMTP_PASSWORD` from `env.secret` and set `SMTP_AUTHENTICATION: ""`. Only
+turn off STARTTLS for an unencrypted relay if you trust the network to it.
+
+### Optional browser push notifications
+
+Generate a VAPID key pair using the [development guide](development.md#web-push-notifications).
+Uncomment `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` in both `env.secret` and your
+`.kamal/secrets`, then fill in the generated values. Keep the same pair across
+deploys. Email and background jobs work without these keys.
+
+## Deploy
+
+Commit your application and deployment configuration changes. Kamal builds from
+Git, so uncommitted application changes are not included in the image by default.
+Then run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+`bin/kamal` uses the bundled Kamal version (you can also use `bundle exec kamal`).
+It builds and pushes the image, installs the proxy, and boots Fizzy. The image's
+entrypoint prepares all SQLite databases and runs migrations before starting the
+web server and its Solid Queue processes.
+
+Open `https://your-hostname` and sign up. Check that the verification email
+arrives. If deployment or mail delivery fails, inspect `bin/kamal logs`. You can
+also use `bin/kamal console` and `bin/kamal shell` for troubleshooting.
+
+For subsequent releases, commit your changes and run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+## Persistent data and backups
+
+The named Docker volume `fizzy_storage` is mounted at `/rails/storage`. It holds
+all four production SQLite databases (primary, cable, cache, and queue), including
+pending jobs, plus local uploads in `storage/production/files`. Replacing the
+application container during a deploy does not replace this volume. Keep its
+name and mount path unchanged; do not delete it or prune it as unused storage.
+
+**Persistence is not a backup.** Back up the volume and your secrets off-server.
+Stop the app (including its workers) for a consistent filesystem backup, or use
+SQLite-aware backup tools that account for WAL files. Test restoring both the
+databases and uploads. This single-server setup does not provide replication or
+failover if the server or its disk is lost.
diff --git a/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb b/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a55420f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/test/lib/deployment_configuration_test.rb
@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@
+require "test_helper"
+require "kamal"
+require "open3"
+require "tmpdir"
+
+class DeploymentConfigurationTest < ActiveSupport::TestCase
+  test "single-server deployment uses the proxy and runs jobs in the web container" do
+    assert_equal [ "web" ], deployment.roles.map(&:name)
+    assert_equal 1, deployment.app_hosts.size
+    assert_empty deployment.accessories
+    assert deployment.proxy.ssl?
+    assert_equal 80, deployment.proxy.app_port
+    assert_equal "/up", deployment.proxy.proxy_config.dig("healthcheck", "path")
+    assert_equal deployment.proxy.hosts.first, deployment.env.clear["APP_FQDN"]
+    assert_equal "true", deployment.env.clear["SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA"]
+    assert_equal "sqlite", deployment.env.clear["DATABASE_ADAPTER"]
+    assert_equal "local", deployment.env.clear["ACTIVE_STORAGE_SERVICE"]
+    assert_includes deployment.raw_config.volumes, "fizzy_storage:/rails/storage"
+    assert_equal "/rails/public/assets", deployment.raw_config.asset_path
+  end
+
+  test "example secrets supply the application and registry without embedding credentials" do
+    values = {
+      "KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD" => "test-registry-token",
+      "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => SecureRandom.hex(64),
+      "SMTP_USERNAME" => "test-user",
+      "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "test $password # with spaces"
+    }
+    template = Rails.root.join(".kamal/secrets.example").read
+    values.each do |key, value|
+      assert_match(/^#{key}=$/, template)
+      template = template.sub(/^#{key}=$/) { "#{key}='#{value}'" }
+    end
+
+    Dir.mktmpdir do |directory|
+      secrets_path = File.join(directory, "secrets")
+      File.write(secrets_path, template)
+      config = Kamal::Configuration.new(deployment.raw_config.to_h.merge(secrets_path: secrets_path), version: "test")
+
+      assert_equal values["KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD"], config.registry.password
+      config.env.secret_keys.each do |key|
+        assert_equal values.fetch(key), config.env.to_h.fetch(key)
+        refute config.env.clear.key?(key)
+      end
+    end
+  end
+
+  test "local secrets are ignored by Git and excluded from Docker builds" do
+    %w[ .kamal/secrets .kamal/secrets.production .kamal/secrets-common ].each do |path|
+      _, status = Open3.capture2("git", "check-ignore", "--no-index", path, chdir: Rails.root)
+      assert status.success?, "#{path} must be ignored"
+    end
+
+    _, status = Open3.capture2("git", "check-ignore", "--no-index", ".kamal/secrets.example", chdir: Rails.root)
+    refute status.success?, "the example must be safe to commit"
+    assert_includes Rails.root.join(".dockerignore").read.lines.map(&:strip), "/.kamal/"
+  end
+
+  test "production boots with HTTPS links, SMTP, and all data under the persistent mount" do
+    settings = production_settings
+    expected_urls = { "host" => "fizzy.example.test", "protocol" => "https" }
+
+    %w[ mailer_urls controller_urls route_urls ].each do |key|
+      assert_equal expected_urls, settings.fetch(key)
+    end
+    assert_equal "Fizzy <notifications@example.test>", settings["from"]
+    assert_equal "smtp", settings["delivery_method"]
+    assert_equal "smtp.example.test", settings["smtp"]["address"]
+    assert_equal 587, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_equal "example.test", settings["smtp"]["domain"]
+    assert_equal "test-user", settings["smtp"]["user_name"]
+    assert_equal "test-password", settings["smtp"]["password"]
+    assert_equal "plain", settings["smtp"]["authentication"]
+    assert settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+    refute settings["smtp"]["tls"]
+    assert settings["force_ssl"]
+    assert settings["assume_ssl"]
+    assert_equal 200, settings["health_status"]
+    assert_equal "solid_queue", settings["queue_adapter"]
+    assert_equal %w[ cable cache primary queue ], settings["databases"].keys.sort
+    settings["databases"].each_value { |path| assert path.start_with?("storage/"), path }
+    assert_equal Rails.root.join("storage/production/files").to_s, settings["storage"]
+  end
+
+  test "SMTP relays can disable authentication and STARTTLS" do
+    settings = production_settings("SMTP_USERNAME" => nil, "SMTP_PASSWORD" => nil,
+      "SMTP_AUTHENTICATION" => "", "SMTP_PORT" => "25", "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "false",
+      "SMTP_DOMAIN" => nil, "DISABLE_SSL" => "true")
+
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["user_name"]
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["password"]
+    assert_nil settings["smtp"]["authentication"]
+    assert_equal 25, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert_equal "fizzy.example.test", settings["smtp"]["domain"]
+    refute settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+    refute settings["smtp"]["tls"]
+    assert_equal "http", settings["mailer_urls"]["protocol"]
+  end
+
+  test "SMTP supports implicit TLS without STARTTLS" do
+    settings = production_settings("SMTP_PORT" => "465", "SMTP_TLS" => "true", "SMTP_ENABLE_STARTTLS_AUTO" => "false")
+
+    assert_equal 465, settings["smtp"]["port"]
+    assert settings["smtp"]["tls"]
+    refute settings["smtp"]["enable_starttls_auto"]
+  end
+
+  test "production can boot for asset builds without a hostname or runtime secrets" do
+    settings = production_settings("APP_FQDN" => nil, "SMTP_ADDRESS" => nil,
+      "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => nil, "SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY" => "1")
+
+    assert_empty settings["mailer_urls"]
+    assert_equal "localhost", settings["smtp"]["address"]
+    assert_equal 200, settings["health_status"]
+  end
+
+  private
+    def deployment
+      @deployment ||= Kamal::Configuration.create_from(config_file: Rails.root.join("config/deploy.yml"), version: "test")
+    end
+
+    def production_settings(overrides = {})
+      environment = deployment.env.clear.transform_values(&:to_s).merge(
+        "RAILS_ENV" => "production", "BUNDLE_GEMFILE" => Rails.root.join("Gemfile").to_s,
+        "SECRET_KEY_BASE" => SecureRandom.hex(64), "SECRET_KEY_BASE_DUMMY" => nil, "RAILS_MASTER_KEY" => nil,
+        "APP_FQDN" => "fizzy.example.test", "MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS" => "Fizzy <notifications@example.test>",
+        "SMTP_ADDRESS" => "smtp.example.test", "SMTP_DOMAIN" => "example.test",
+        "SMTP_USERNAME" => "test-user", "SMTP_PASSWORD" => "test-password", "SMTP_TLS" => nil,
+        "DISABLE_SSL" => nil, "ASSUME_SSL" => nil, "FORCE_SSL" => nil
+      ).merge(overrides)
+
+      # Boot a fresh production process without changing the test app's environment.
+      # Inspect the transport without opening a connection or sending any mail.
+      script = <<~'CODE'
+        require "json"
+        require "rack/mock"
+        config = Rails.application.config
+        Mail::SMTP.new(ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings).send(:build_smtp_session)
+        status, = Rails.application.call(Rack::MockRequest.env_for("http://127.0.0.1/up"))
+        puts "DEPLOYMENT_SETTINGS=#{JSON.generate({
+          mailer_urls: ActionMailer::Base.default_url_options,
+          controller_urls: ActionController::Base.default_url_options,
+          route_urls: Rails.application.routes.default_url_options,
+          smtp: ActionMailer::Base.smtp_settings,
+          from: ApplicationMailer.default[:from],
+          delivery_method: ActionMailer::Base.delivery_method,
+          storage: ActiveStorage::Blob.service.root.to_s,
+          databases: ActiveRecord::Base.configurations.configs_for(env_name: "production").to_h { |db| [db.name, db.database] },
+          queue_adapter: ActiveJob::Base.queue_adapter_name,
+          force_ssl: config.force_ssl,
+          assume_ssl: config.assume_ssl,
+          health_status: status
+        })}"
+      CODE
+      output, status = Open3.capture2e(environment, Rails.root.join("bin/rails").to_s, "runner", script, chdir: Rails.root)
+      assert status.success?, output
+      result = output.lines.find { |line| line.start_with?("DEPLOYMENT_SETTINGS=") }
+      assert result, output
+      JSON.parse(result.delete_prefix("DEPLOYMENT_SETTINGS="))
+    end
+end
